Pages = {79-86},
Month = {JUN},
Abstract = {The study discusses how IFRS's objective of the harmonization of
   accounting standards and improvement of quality of financial reporting
   may have been negatively affected due to public authorities influences
   in the European Union (EU), the U.S., the U.K. and China. In addition,
   we discuss issues related to the inconsistent interpretations and
   implementations of IFRS as principle-based accounting standards.
   Moreover, we discuss how the funding system of the IASB may (or may not)
