   overview of the current literature, and guide for the treating
   dermatopathologist},
Journal = {AMERICAN JOURNAL OF DERMATOPATHOLOGY},
Year = {2003},
Volume = {25},
Number = {4},
Pages = {321-326},
Month = {AUG},
Abstract = {We describe a case of cutaneous leishmaniasis in a Spanish patient
   visiting Los Angeles. Leishmania species cause both cutaneous and
   visceral disease; the majority of infections with Leishmania are of the
   cutaneous form. Although leishmaniasis is a relatively rare occurrence
   in the United States, travel by United States' citizens to endemic
   regions and increased United States military operations in the Middle
   East raise the chances of encountering cutaneous leishmaniasis. The
   following case report and overview of the current literature outlines
   the major morphologic findings and current diagnostic modalities
   available to diagnose cutaneous leishmaniasis.},
