   Utilit; Environm Assessment Assoc; Int Eros Control Assoc; Natl Onsite
   Wastewater Recycling Assoc; SE Public Serv Authority; USN; Old Dominion
   Univ},
Abstract = {This paper presents an overview of the new ASCE Technical Guidance
   Document entitled ``Management of leachate from Sanitary Landfills.{''}
   The text, prepared by a team of solid waste professionals representing
   academia, industry and private practice, provides a comprehensive
   overview of all aspects of the management of leachate from a modem lined
   Municipal Solid Waste (MSW) landfill. The peer-reviewed Technical
   Guidance Document includes sections on:
   Characterization of MSWLeachate
   Generation
   Pumping
   Storage
   Management Options, and
   Emerging and Innovative Treatment
   The potential audience for this document includes practicing
   professionals, educators, students and the regulatory community. The
   document, by design, has a practical, rather than an academic emphasis.
   Leachate management is an important issue for owner/operators as it
   represents a significant cost of operation, both active and
   post-closure. It is also an important issue from an environmental,
   standpoint, since leachate is one of the primary routes of off-site
   migration and contaminant transport from a landfill if not properly
   managed. It is the hope of the authors that this Technical Guidance
   Document will contribute toward this goal.},
